WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:25.960
- [Mark] All right T.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.240
T where are you from originally?

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.073
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:28.073 --> 00:00:28.906
- [T] Compton.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:30.983
- [Mark] Tell me about your family.

00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:32.270
You grew up with both of your parents?

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.743
- Yeah, went to school,
was brought up nice,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.690
but somehow I end up bad.
(Mark chuckles)

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.993
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.793
- Shit, I didn't have no childhood really.

00:00:50.045 --> 00:00:52.800
I started fucking up when I was like 15

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.770
and I've been fucking up ever since,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:57.824
they tried to raise me
right but somehow...

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:58.657
- [Mark] So your parents were good

00:00:58.657 --> 00:00:59.663
and they were there for you,

00:00:59.663 --> 00:01:01.920
but you just kinda went
a different direction?

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:02.753
- Yeah.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.333
- [Mark] What age were you

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:06.868
when you left your parents' house?

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.283
- 17.
- [Mark] 17?

00:01:08.283 --> 00:01:09.116
- Yeah.

00:01:09.116 --> 00:01:10.170
- [Mark] Where'd you go from there?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.173
- Job Corps, I fucked up there,

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.423
went to the military.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:22.710
I got an honorable discharge, then shit,

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.933
I just been fucking up, I
don't know what's wrong.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:26.900
- [Mark] What eh...

00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:32.550
You're now a pimp for some of
the girls here on Skid Row?

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.383
- Yap.

00:01:33.383 --> 00:01:34.400
- [Mark] One of the
girls is Candace, right?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.060
- Yeah.
- [Mark] I know Candace.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.340
Is this something that you saw as a kid?

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.540
You saw guys doing that in
your neighborhood stuff like?

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.053
- No.
- [Mark] No?

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.830
What do you think led
you down that, to this?

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:46.910
- I needed some money,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.760
shit they was out there doing it,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.443
so I might go be they pimp, you know?

00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:57.766
- [Mark] What's the arrangement?

00:01:57.766 --> 00:01:59.630
The girls work for you,
they bring the money

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:00.893
and then you do what?

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.790
- I break 'em off,

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.373
they only one dope, but
I give them money too,

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.730
they stay with me, some of them.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:13.990
- [Mark] Yeah, I went by your tent.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.563
You got like three girls
living with you, right?

00:02:15.563 --> 00:02:18.000
- Yeah, I was wrong.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.300
I think I'm getting tired,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.990
I'm trynna get out of downtown,

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.290
it's kinda rough,

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.260
I've been down here like five years.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.310
- [Mark] Yeah, have you done prison time?

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.358
- Yeah.

00:02:34.358 --> 00:02:36.031
- [Mark] What kinda stuff
you been in prison for?

00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:40.310
- Shit, robbery, attempted murder,

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.000
I just got out.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.330
I've been out five years, I got out.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.418
I did 18 years, straight.

00:02:47.418 --> 00:02:49.043
- [Mark] What for?
- Robbery.

00:02:49.043 --> 00:02:51.043
- [Mark] Robbery?
- Yeah.

00:02:53.337 --> 00:02:54.700
- [Mark] Do you have kids of your own?

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.960
- Two girls.
- [Mark] Did you raise them?

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.560
- When I went to prison they
was like about seven and nine

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.380
and I ain't seen them in all them years.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.250
When I got out I tried to talk to them,

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.100
but they act like they don't know me,

00:03:11.225 --> 00:03:13.930
they was acting like I was
a stranger or something.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:14.763
- [Mark] Right.

00:03:14.763 --> 00:03:18.333
- So, I don't talk with them no more.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.863
I had a place but, some girl burned it.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.090
So, I got a place last year,

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.790
I was only in there for nine days,

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.550
she burned it, they kicked me out.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:36.780
I'm trying to find another
place, but it's hard.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.613
- [Mark] Yeah,

00:03:39.877 --> 00:03:42.390
what are the personality traits
you need to work as a pimp?

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:47.390
You need to have what traits
to get a girl to work for you?

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:52.503
- Oh, charisma, you gotta have, finesse,

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.093
you gotta treat them right.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.353
If they treat you right,
you gotta treat them right.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:08.813
- [Mark] Does force

00:04:08.813 --> 00:04:11.210
or intimidation come into
the picture sometimes?

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.450
- [T] Not with me.
- [Mark] Not with you?

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.450
- [T] Yeah, if they don't wanna
do it then I ain't gon' trip

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.960
I ain't gon' turn nobody out,
if they doing it already.

00:04:23.979 --> 00:04:26.629
- [Mark] What are the traits
a girl needs to do this,

00:04:27.677 --> 00:04:28.940
to work for you?

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.240
- [T] She gotta look good.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:32.483
She gotta act right,

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.063
that's about it.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:41.733
And don't be stealing,

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.243
get a man what he paying for,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.860
that way won't be no problems.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.190
- [Mark] What are your plans
down the road, for the future?

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.963
Do you have anything
you'd like to see happen?

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.556
- Four more months,

00:05:00.556 --> 00:05:02.773
that's my goal to be outta downtown.

00:05:05.818 --> 00:05:08.190
- [Mark] Are you using any of
the drugs that are out here?

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.823
- I use a little bit of
crystal, I got to stay up.

00:05:15.619 --> 00:05:18.743
- [Mark] How much do the
girls bring in at night?

00:05:18.743 --> 00:05:20.731
- 500,
- [Mark] How much?

00:05:20.731 --> 00:05:22.590
- 500
- [Mark] Per girl?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.003
- Yeah.
- [Mark] That's pretty good.

00:05:25.003 --> 00:05:27.460
- I don't, keep my girls down here,

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.730
they ain't gonna make shit down here.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.510
- [Mark] Better neighborhoods
for making money, right?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.343
- Yeah.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.470
- [Mark] Where do you guys go, Figueroa?

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:37.574
- I go to Hollywood
- [Mark] Hollywood?

00:05:37.574 --> 00:05:39.074
- Yeah
- [Mark] Like Western?

00:05:40.054 --> 00:05:42.971
- Western, there's a lot of places.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:51.093
I go to the beach
sometimes, to The Valley.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.950
'Cause down here, it ain't nothing but...

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:01.603
If I was a girl,

00:06:01.603 --> 00:06:03.140
I wouldn't do nothing down here.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:04.430
- [Mark] Right? Yeah.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.647
You make, you make a
fraction of the money, right?

00:06:09.945 --> 00:06:13.625
- Or John end up kicking your
ass taking the money back

00:06:13.625 --> 00:06:14.710
and don't give you nothing at all.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.513
- [Mark] Yeah, it's crazy our here.

00:06:16.513 --> 00:06:17.346
- Yeah.

00:06:20.592 --> 00:06:22.842
(sniffles)

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.984
- [Mark] All right,
well T thank you so much

00:06:25.984 --> 00:06:26.884
for talking to me.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.310
- What'd you do?

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.530
- I'm a photographer.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:34.610
I just find these stories down
here interesting. (chuckles)

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:36.477
Everybody's got an interesting
story to tell, like you do.

00:06:36.477 --> 00:06:37.980
- You don't go nowhere else?

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.010
- [Mark] What do you mean?
The neighborhoods?

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.105
Oh yeah.
Yeah. I go all around.

00:06:42.105 --> 00:06:44.010
I've been down here cause it's just like,

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.310
every time I come down here,
there's more interesting stuff.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.963
Like you, you just walked
into my lap today, right?

00:06:48.963 --> 00:06:49.796
- Yeah.

00:06:49.796 --> 00:06:50.700
- [Mark] This neighborhood is charged full

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.890
of interesting people like you,

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.030
but one day and sometimes
I go to other neighborhoods

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.290
and find interesting stuff elsewhere too.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.430
'Cause there's stuff like this going on,

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.100
all over the country,
- Yeah

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.370
- [Mark] Not just right here in Skid Row,

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:08.400
but Skid Row does have a ton of it.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.790
So I don't have to work too hard,

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:10.623
I just show up here
(T chuckles)

00:07:10.623 --> 00:07:14.390
and it falls into my lap,
but I've been to other places

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.879
and it's probably time to st--

00:07:16.879 --> 00:07:19.230
- What you doing in life?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.080
- [Mark] What am I doing tonight?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.650
- Nope. I mean,

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:22.640
- [Mark] Going to Lakers game.(chuckles)

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.500
- No, what you do in life?

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.333
- [Mark] Oh in life,
What did you become?

00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:27.990
- [Mark] I'm a photographer.
- That's what you been doing--

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.260
- [Mark] Yeah, I support
myself shooting advertising,

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.920
photography, for companies that need ads

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.110
and stuff like that,

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:37.920
that's how I make money, I
don't make money doing this,

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.793
I bleed money doing this,
but I find it interesting.

00:07:41.758 --> 00:07:44.280
- So you making money and
just like giving it away?

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.990
- [Mark] I'm basically
giving it away, yeah.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.230
- You don't really need it?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.940
- [Mark] No, money is important,
I don't wanna give it away,

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.283
but I don't think you
would come in here for $5.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.080
- Shit, if I was desperate I would.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.420
- [Mark] Yeah, so I have to
end up paying people like you,

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.570
to come in here,

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.820
and sometimes that costs
me 20 bucks or more.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.190
People like you, I probably
have to pay quite a bit more

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.610
than 20, but a lot of the heroin addicts

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:11.443
that are out here in the street,

00:08:11.443 --> 00:08:14.973
that are doing the craziest stuff,

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.750
are happy to come in here for 20 bucks

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.450
and I'm happy to pay 'em for that.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:21.650
I have them sign a release,

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:24.993
we do a little talk and
I put it on YouTube.

00:08:26.037 --> 00:08:26.930
- And people see it?

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:27.763
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.000
I'm very new at it so it's like,

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:35.400
I started off with getting
like 12 or 15 views a day,

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.970
and now, it's growing and
it's growing pretty quickly.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.860
So it's kind of encouraging
to see people kind of,

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.200
some people can't watch this stuff.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.500
It's just too dark. (chuckles)

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.323
It's too disturbing, but
other people will find it,

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.670
I think you can learn a
lot about human nature,

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:55.190
you can learn a lot about what's
going on with our society,

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:56.960
you can find out about
some of the problems

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.643
that we have as a country,
by watching these things,

00:09:02.652 --> 00:09:04.530
'cause it's a complex problem.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.110
It's racism, it's wealth inequality,

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:10.160
it's opportunity and education inequality,

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:11.730
it's self-esteem issues,

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:12.847
it's self worth, it's everything.

00:09:12.847 --> 00:09:16.013
- I think the government is causing this.

00:09:17.952 --> 00:09:20.422
- [Mark] The government
is a huge part of it.

00:09:20.422 --> 00:09:24.533
Because, the black
community is so beaten down,

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.680
like I talk to some of these gang kids

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:28.513
and they're like,

00:09:28.513 --> 00:09:31.121
"What options did you
have as a kid?" (chuckles)

00:09:31.121 --> 00:09:32.320
"I didn't have any", you know?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.970
when I was a kid growing
up in suburban Chicago--

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.040
- Well, back in our day

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.980
I don't think we really had non, but now

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.290
I think the young kids, if
they wanna do something right,

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:47.350
they got opportunities and shit.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.310
- [Mark] Well, I mean,
they do and they don't,

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:52.037
it's still really rough
for a lot of people.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.580
In certain neighborhoods,
it's just it's so...

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.413
- Yeah.

00:10:00.413 --> 00:10:03.420
- [Mark] So bleak, there's so few chances,

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:06.390
when I grew up I could
have been a lawyer, doctor,

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.590
politician, I chose photographer,

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.480
but I could have done anything.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.300
A lot of these kids I talked to were like,

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.480
they didn't have a chance in hell.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.680
They didn't know what a
photographer looked like,

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:18.070
or a doctor or a lawyer, they didn't know,

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.420
how would you even do that?

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:24.470
- So, what I see is,

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.775
there's no hope for the
black people no more.

00:10:26.775 --> 00:10:29.182
- [Mark] That's what I'm
saying, they don't have hope.

00:10:29.182 --> 00:10:30.432
- I mean, shit.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.605
- [Mark] That needs to change.

00:10:36.605 --> 00:10:37.900
- Shit, it ain't gon' change.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.890
I remember when I was
in junior high school,

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:45.890
I used to come down on May
and it was homeless then,

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.903
but I didn't know about it.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.170
I didn't think it,

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.510
I seen people hanging out
on the streets, sleeping.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.060
I didn't think nothing about homelessness,

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.783
but shit, it was there,

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:03.559
and shit, then I did 18 years
in prison and it's still here.

00:11:03.559 --> 00:11:05.241
- [Mark] It's still here.

00:11:05.241 --> 00:11:07.158
- It's not gon' change,

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.110
- [Mark] What I'm hoping is
by putting out these videos,

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.110
maybe creating a little bit of awareness,

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:18.870
about how bad it is and how
how tough it is for some people

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.840
and how they got that way.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.280
Like, how does a girl end
up as a heroin addict,

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.390
as a crack addict on the street,

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:31.390
selling her body to make a
buck and that's her only,

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.490
given up her kids and that's her life,

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.640
and she has no hope for anything better,

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:38.960
nothing, no miracle is gonna
come out of the woodwork

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.000
and save her life.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.270
- 'Cause she's used to
this, that's all she knows.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.090
- [Mark] A lot of it is a self worth,

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.980
that they didn't ever develop,

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.720
because their parents
treated them like crap

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.400
or abandoned them and
they were in foster homes.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.600
- They guy beating them
up and that kinda shit.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.910
- [Mark] They were
molested at six years old,

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:55.423
they were in foster homes, they had crap.

00:11:57.158 --> 00:11:59.520
I had supportive parents, I
had parents that loved me,

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:00.353
they still do.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.600
They were consistent,

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.970
so I had that wonderful upbringing

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:09.010
that a lot of the people
I'm talking to, (chuckles)

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:11.750
they wouldn't even know
what that looked like.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.550
They have no idea.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.293
They didn't even know their parents,

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:18.540
the foster home treated them like crap

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.970
and they ran away from the
foster home as teenagers

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.910
and they grew up in the street.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.200
What does a young girl do
on the street to make money?

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.100
'Cause she needs money, right?

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.853
There you go.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:31.610
That's a terrible thing
that goes on in our society

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:32.600
and it goes on a lot,

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.600
people just would rather not look at it.

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:38.620
So I'm putting out these
painful, hard to look at videos--

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.880
- The people at the top
know what is going on.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:42.770
- [Mark] I think a lot of people

